Theorem: All potions are the same color.

Proof by induction:

1) One potion is obviously the same color.

2) Assume K potions are the same color.  Consider a group of K+1
potions. Remove one potion from the group; the remaining K potions are,
by assumption, the same color. Replace the removed potion and remove
another potion.  The remaining K potions are again, by assumption, the
same color. Repeat with each of the K+1 sets of K potions.  Since all
K+1 sets of K potions are the same color, we can deduce that K+1
potions are the same color.

3) Since SameColor(1) is true, and SameColor(K) implies SameColor(K+1),
induction lets us conclude that SameColor(N) is true for all N >= 1.
Q.E.D.



